title: What If an AI Ran Your Country? (sample)   (AI điều hành quốc gia — bản mẫu)
channel: ifm
format: vertical
run: 1
next: What if money disappeared?
voice: am_puck
people: facet
sources: Albania "Diella" AI minister, 11 Sep 2025 (Global Government Forum; bne IntelliNews). Everything else is the imagined simulation.

// S01 · HOOK — 3D city at midnight
# vis kind=w act=s3 set=city time=night cam=EWS.high.orbit on=center words="WHAT IF AN AI@0|RAN YOUR COUNTRY?@1" then="cam=WS.low.pull on=tower@2"
Midnight. A whole country hands its government to an artificial intelligence.
No president. No parliament. One machine.
So what actually happens next?

// S02 · DAY ONE — the plaza
# vis kind=w act=s3 set=plaza time=day do=sign n=36 cam=EWS.low.crane on=building trans=zoomthru then="cam=WS.high.orbit on=crowd@1|cam=MS.eye.push on=crowd@2"
Day one. A crowd gathers outside parliament.
Some are cheering. Some brought signs.
Most just want to know if anyone is still inside.

// S03 · REAL — this is not pure fiction
# vis kind=w act=map view=tilt pins="20,41.2,ALBANIA" cam=WS.high.push:.5,.45 trans=slide words="~AI MINISTER@1|2025@2" then="cam=CU.eye.push:.6,.37@1"
This isn't pure fiction.
In 2025, Albania named an AI called Diella as a minister for public tenders.
A virtual official, still inside a human government.

// S04 · THE QUEUE — boring, and huge
# vis kind=w act=s3 set=waiting time=day screen="NOW SERVING|NO QUEUE" cam=WS.high.trackL on=chairs trans=fade then="cam=MS.eye.push on=screen@1|empty=1 cam=WS.high.static on=chairs@2"
In our imaginary country, the first change is boring, and huge.
The queue at the tax office?
Gone by morning.

// S05 · ANA
# vis kind=w act=s3 set=home time=dawn cam=WS.eye.pull on=room trans=ink then="cam=MCU.low.push on=her@1|cam=CU.high.static on=phone@2"
Ana, a nurse, wakes up to a message.
The permit she has waited months for
was approved at three in the morning.

// S06 · WHAT PEOPLE SAY — the theory
# vis kind=w act=s3 set=street time=day cam=WS.eye.trackR on=street do=phone trans=slide then="cam=MS.low.push on=her@1|act=s3 set=servers cam=WS.eye.push on=aisle@2|cam=MCU.dutch.orbit on=rack@3"
By lunch, a theory is everywhere online.
The machine wasn't switched on last night. It had been quietly running things for years.
There is no evidence for that.
But it hides a real question: when the machine is wrong, who do you complain to?
